        "id": "mpv-iconv",
        "release": "rn-media task #32 (parity release)",
        "how": "Aligned DOWN: darwin now passes -Diconv=disabled, matching Android. Android builds at API 21 and bionic only gained iconv(3) at API 28, so enabling it there would need minSdk 28 (dropping Android 5-8) or vendoring GNU libiconv. With uchardet disabled and --metadata-codepage unset on both forks, mp_iconv_to_utf8() returns its buffer untouched anyway, so this was inert on iOS. THE LOSS: neither platform can now apply an explicit --metadata-codepage. Restoring it on BOTH is tracked in rn-media task #32."
      }
    ],
    "notes": [
      "The darwin scope is the iOS effective set: DISABLE_ALL_OPTIONS then COMMON_OPTIONS then IOS_OPTIONS,",
      "with later values winning, which is what meson sees. The macOS-only additions (-Dcoreaudio=enabled,",
      "-Dcocoa=enabled) are not part of what rn-media ships and are deliberately not recorded here.",
      "",
      "Export control is NOT in this list because the two forks do it with different mechanisms: Android",
      "passes -Wl,--version-script=include/mpv.ver plus -Wl,--exclude-libs=ALL through -Dc_link_args, and",
      "darwin does it with a PATCH (005-mpv-export-list) that edits library('mpv')'s own link_args. Both",
      "lists live in assets/export-lists/ so the 55-vs-54 delta is visible in one place."
    ]
  }
